#: frontend/src/metabase/reference/segments/SegmentDetail.jsx:48

✨ AI Context
Used in `frontend/src/metabase/reference/segments/SegmentDetail.jsx` as the label for a pre-built question link in the "Useful questions" section of a Segment reference page.
The component builds an array of suggested questions for a given segment:
- One is "Number of {segment.name}" (a count of rows in the segment)
- The other is "See all {segment.name}" (a table view of all rows in the segment)
The placeholder `{0}` corresponds to the segment name (e.g. "active users", "churned accounts"). It is shown as link text in a list of links, not as a button. The surrounding context is explanatory/help UI for analysts viewing documentation about a saved segment, not end users:
[code]
const interestingQuestions = (table, segment, metadata) => {
  return [
    {
      text: t`Number of ${segment.name}`,
      icon: "number",
      link: getQuestionUrl({
        dbId: table && table.db_id,
        tableId: table.id,
        segmentId: segment.id,
        getCount: true,
        metadata,
      }),
    },
    {
      text: t`See all ${segment.name}`,
      icon: "table2",
      link: getQuestionUrl({
        dbId: table && table.db_id,
        tableId: table.id,
        segmentId: segment.id,
        metadata,
      }),
    },
  ];
};
[/code]
So translations like "See all {0}" / "View all {0}" that refer to viewing all rows/items in that segment are appropriate.
✨ 🔚

#: enterprise/frontend/src/metabase-enterprise/dependencies/utils.ts:52
#: enterprise/frontend/src/metabase-enterprise/dependencies/utils.ts:565


✨ AI Context
In `enterprise/frontend/src/metabase-enterprise/dependencies/utils.ts`, the string "Row and column security rule" is used as the *fallback label* for dependency graph nodes of type `sandbox` (which represent row/column security rules) when there is no `table.display_name` set on the node. It appears in the function `getNodeLabel(node: DependencyNode): string`, which controls how nodes are labeled in the Enterprise dependency graph UI.
Relevant code:
```ts
export function getNodeLabel(node: DependencyNode): string {
  switch (node.type) {
    case "table":
      return node.data.display_name;
    case "sandbox":
      return node.data.table?.display_name ?? t`Row and column security rule`;
    default:
      return node.data.name;
  }
}
```
✨ 🔚

