#: frontend/src/metabase/lib/utils.ts:24


✨ AI Context
In `frontend/src/metabase/lib/utils.ts`, the string `seven` is used inside the `numberToWord(num: number)` utility function as part of a list of localized number words for digits 0–9:
```ts
export function numberToWord(num: number) {
  const names = [
    t`zero`,
    t`one`,
    t`two`,
    t`three`,
    t`four`,
    t`five`,
    t`six`,
    t`seven`,
    t`eight`,
    t`nine`,
  ];
  if (num >= 0 && num <= 9) {
    return names[num];
  } else {
    return "" + num;
  }
}
```
The string is the localized word for the digit 7, used when converting small integer values (0–9) to their word equivalents in the Metabase UI. It will appear wherever the app needs to display a numeric digit as a word rather than as a numeral.
✨ 🔚

