#, javascript-format

✨ AI Context
This string is used as the name (label) of a command in the command palette, when search typeahead is disabled. It appears as an action item that users can select to navigate to the full search page.
Code:
In `frontend/src/metabase/palette/hooks/useCommandPalette.tsx`:
```
const searchResultActions = useMemo<PaletteAction[]>(() => {
  ...
  const searchLocation = {
    pathname: "search",
    query: {
      ...locationQuery,
      q: debouncedSearchText,
    },
  };
  if (!isSearchTypeaheadEnabled) {
    return [
      {
        id: `search-without-typeahead`,
        name: t`View search results for "${debouncedSearchText}"`,
        section: "search",
        keywords: debouncedSearchText,
        icon: "link" as const,
        priority: Priority.HIGH,
        extra: {
          href: searchLocation,
        },
      },
    ];
  }
  ...
}, [...]);
```
`{0}` corresponds to the current search query text (`debouncedSearchText`) entered by the user in the command palette search field. The command appears under the "search" section with a link icon, and when selected, it takes the user to the `/search` page with the query applied.
✨ 🔚

