#: frontend/src/metabase/account/notifications/components/ArchiveModal/ArchiveModal.jsx:119

✨ AI Context
This string is shown in the archive confirmation modal for alerts and subscriptions in the account notifications UI.
In `frontend/src/metabase/account/notifications/components/ArchiveModal/ArchiveModal.jsx`, the helper function `getDateMessage` builds the message using the alert's creation date:
[code]
const getDateMessage = (item, type) => {
  const options = Settings.formattingOptions();
  const createdAt = formatDateTimeWithUnit(item.created_at, "day", options);
  switch (type) {
    case "alert":
      return t`You created this alert on ${createdAt}. `;
    case "pulse":
      return t`You created this subscription on ${createdAt}. `;
  }
};
[/code]
- **When it appears**: In the `ArchiveModal` component when a user is archiving (canceling) an alert they previously created.
- **What {0} represents**: The formatted `created_at` date of the alert item, e.g. "June 15, 2024".
- **Surrounding text**: This sentence is combined with other messages about no longer receiving the alert and who currently receives it, forming a full explanation in the archive modal.
✨ 🔚

#: frontend/src/metabase/dashboard/components/DashCard/DashCardParameterMapper/DashCardCardParameterMapperContent.tsx:109


✨ AI Context
In `DashCardCardParameterMapperContent.tsx`, this string is used as the header text of the parameter-mapping panel when the dashboard parameter is a temporal (time-based) unit. It appears above controls that let the user choose which field or variable the parameter should connect to.
Code context:
```ts
const headerContent = useMemo(() => {
  if (layoutHeight <= 2) {
    return null;
  }
  if (isTemporalUnit) {
    return t`Connect to`;
  }
  if (!isVirtual && !(isNative && isDisabled)) {
    return t`Column to filter on`;
  }
  return t`Variable to map to`;
}, [layoutHeight, isTemporalUnit, isVirtual, isNative, isDisabled]);
```
