#: enterprise/frontend/src/embedding-sdk/components/private/PublicComponentWrapper/SdkError.tsx:47
#, javascript-format

✨ AI Context
This string is used in the embedding SDK error UI when a requested resource (question, dashboard, collection, etc.) cannot be found by the ID provided to the SDK.
In `frontend/src/embedding-sdk-bundle/components/private/PublicComponentWrapper/SdkError.tsx`, the translation-key form of this message is constructed via `jt` as:
```tsx
const ResourceNotFoundError = ({
  resource,
  id,
}: ResourceNotFoundErrorProps & { resource: string }) => (
  <SdkError
    message={jt`${resource} ${(
      <Code
        bg="background-error-secondary"
        c="text-secondary"
        key="question-id"
      >
        {id}
      </Code>
    )} not found. Make sure you pass the correct ID.`}
  />
);
export const QuestionNotFoundError = ({ id }: ResourceNotFoundErrorProps) => (
  <ResourceNotFoundError resource={t`Question`} id={id} />
);
export const DashboardNotFoundError = ({ id }: ResourceNotFoundErrorProps) => (
  <ResourceNotFoundError resource={t`Dashboard`} id={id} />
);
export const CollectionNotFoundError = ({ id }: ResourceNotFoundErrorProps) => (
  <ResourceNotFoundError resource={t`Collection`} id={id} />
);
```
At runtime this appears in an in-app error banner or inline error state in embedded Metabase content. `{0}` corresponds to the resource type label (e.g. `Question`, `Dashboard`, `Collection`), and `{1}` corresponds to the ID value that failed lookup. The ID is rendered in a monospace `Code` UI component to visually distinguish it as a technical identifier. The message guides developers integrating the SDK to check that they are passing the correct ID for the requested resource.
✨ 🔚

#: frontend/src/metabase/admin/settings/components/UploadSettings/UploadSettingsForm.tsx:221


✨ AI Context
In `frontend/src/metabase/admin/settings/components/UploadSettings/UploadSettingsForm.tsx`, this string is used as the `label` of a `TextInput` field that appears only when `showPrefix` is true in the Upload Settings admin UI. The full JSX snippet:
```tsx
{showPrefix && (
  <TextInput
    label={t`Upload Table Prefix (optional)`}
    value={tablePrefix ?? ""}
    placeholder={t`upload_`}
    onChange={(e) => {
      resetButtons();
      setTablePrefix(e.target.value);
    }}
  />
)}
```
This field lets an admin specify an optional string prefix (e.g. `upload_`) that will be added to the names of tables created by the uploads feature. It is shown in the Metabase Admin > Settings > Uploads configuration form.
✨ 🔚

