#: metabase/lib/filter.cljc:221 metabase/lib/filter.cljc:224
✨ AI Context This string is used when generating a human-readable description of a filter condition in query builders and filter pills. In `src/metabase/lib/filter.cljc`, it appears in the branch for the `:contains` operator when there is exactly one value: `[:contains _ x & args] (if (= (count args) 1) (let [y (first args)] (i18n/tru "{0} contains {1}" (->display-name x) (if (string? y) y (->display-name y)))) (i18n/tru "{0} contains {1} selections" ...))` - **{0}** is the display name of the field or dimension being filtered (e.g. a column name like "Product Name"). - **{1}** is the single value the field must contain; it is either the raw string value or the display name of another field/variable. This text is shown anywhere Metabase renders textual descriptions of filters, such as filter summaries above a question, filter chips, or sidebar filter descriptions in the UI. ✨ 🔚
